  </questionnote>
  <questiondescription format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p id="concept">Integration: finding the constant of integration from a starting value</p><p id="description">Grade 12 CBE Core 4.2: Integrate a rate of change, use the starting value to find the constant, and evaluate the amount at a later time.</p><p id="edition">Core</p><p id="provenance">This question is adapted from Exercise D, Question 7 in Chapter 10 of Cassell, D., Instone, S., Ling, J., Scruton, P., Shilton, S. and West, H., SMP AS/A2 Mathematics: Core 1 for AQA, Cambridge University Press, 2004: new Kenyan contexts (a tank in Kitui, a seedling in Kakamega) and new numbers.</p><p id="citation">INNODEMS CBC Grade 12 Mathematics, first draft by Ben Davies, 2026. Aligned to the KICD Senior School Curriculum Design, Core Mathematics Grade 12 (draft).</p>]]></text></questiondescription>
